CompanyWrt notices and upstream license sources
================================================

CompanyWrt-authored files in this repository, including the LuCI dashboard
overlay, build/verification scripts and configuration templates, are distributed
under the repository MIT License unless a file says otherwise. The vendored
Liquid theme is a separate upstream work and is not covered by that MIT grant.

The firmware is assembled from official OpenWrt 25.12.5 binary packages. Those
packages are separate upstream works and retain their own copyright/license
terms. The generated package manifest and CycloneDX SBOM are the authoritative
per-build inventory; APK metadata inside the image records package licenses.
The AX9000 Darkyun RC5 build verifies one-to-one inventory coverage from all
214 resolved APK
package names to CycloneDX upstream components. This is not a claim that every
license conclusion is complete: when OpenWrt omits a source component or
license assertion (notably the libnghttp2-14 package in 25.12.5), the augmented
SBOM records an inventory component with `NOASSERTION`. Consult the pinned APK
metadata, corresponding source archive and license files before redistribution.
Key upstream source/license locations are:

* OpenWrt build system/base — GPL-2.0-only; additional package licenses apply:
  https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/blob/openwrt-25.12/COPYING
  https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/tree/openwrt-25.12/LICENSES
* Official target binaries, package repositories, profiles and source archives:
  https://downloads.openwrt.org/releases/25.12.5/
* LuCI and luci-proto-wireguard — Apache-2.0:
  https://github.com/openwrt/luci/blob/openwrt-25.12/LICENSE
* luci-theme-liquid — pinned source commit
  `ad0cce67c02ce9ce0154c2f08491fc8ac1daf06b`:
  https://github.com/zzsj0928/luci-theme-liquid
  The repository-level LICENSE says GPL-3.0 while its Makefile, README and
  individual source headers say Apache-2.0. CompanyWrt preserves those notices
  and conservatively declares the vendored APK and CompanyWrt patch component
  GPL-3.0-only until upstream resolves the mismatch. The complete GPL-3.0 text
  is installed at `/usr/share/licenses/luci-theme-liquid/LICENSE`.
* pbr — AGPL-3.0-or-later (package metadata and source):
  https://github.com/openwrt/packages/blob/openwrt-25.12/net/pbr/Makefile
  https://github.com/mossdef-org/pbr/
* WireGuard tools — GPL-2.0:
  https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/blob/openwrt-25.12/package/network/utils/wireguard-tools/Makefile
  https://git.zx2c4.com/wireguard-tools/
* sqm-scripts (optional, not preinstalled) — GPL-2.0-only:
  https://github.com/openwrt/packages/blob/openwrt-25.12/net/sqm-scripts/Makefile
  https://github.com/tohojo/sqm-scripts
* usign — ISC:
  https://git.openwrt.org/project/usign.git

OpenClash itself, its mihomo core, subscriptions and rule data are not included.
Its runtime dependencies are also absent from the lean base and are resolved
only during a separately reviewed installation; see docs/openclash.md.

The pinned `packages/luci-theme-liquid` source is compiled as a real
`luci-theme-liquid` APK by the fixed OpenWrt Buildroot and therefore appears in
PACKAGE-MANIFEST and the upstream SBOM mapping. Its CompanyWrt-specific patch is
also inventoried separately. `luci-app-company` and operational files continue
to be copied as named `*-overlay` components and are explicitly represented in
CUSTOM-COMPONENTS.manifest, the release manifest, NOTICE and augmented SBOM.
